  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement I : Iron (III) catalyst, acidified <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> and neutral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> have the ability to oxidise <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;independently.</p><p>Statement II: Manganate ion is paramagnetic in nature and involves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>p&#960;</mi></math> bonding.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LK7b9",
      "text": "Both statement I and Statement II are ture",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
